6 0 obj
<< /Length 2667 >>
stream
BT
/F1 9 Tf
12 TL
1 0 0 1 36 806 Tm
(A3. POOL BUDGETS) Tj
T*
(  A pool budget is the active pool_budgets row of the capacity workbook) Tj
T*
(  with the highest revision_seq. A budget whose scale_unit reads) Tj
T*
(  milli_tick is converted with budget_ticks = ceil\(budget_value / 1000\).) Tj
T*
(  The net budget of a pool is its budget_ticks less the reservation of) Tj
T*
(  every active maintenance window naming that pool, each window converted) Tj
T*
(  by its own field name, and never below 0.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A4. ADMISSION ORDER AND THE SELECTION OBJECTIVE) Tj
T*
(  Pools are admitted in bytewise order of pool_id.) Tj
T*
(  Inside one pool the candidate order is the tuple) Tj
T*
(    \(priority_class, closure_cost, unit_id\)) Tj
T*
(  ascending, compared bytewise on unit_id. closure_cost is the summed cost) Tj
T*
(  of the candidate's own prerequisite closure, counting only members not) Tj
T*
(  already selected.) Tj
T*
(  A candidate is admitted only with its whole prerequisite closure: the) Tj
T*
(  candidate plus every dirty unit of the same target reachable from it) Tj
T*
(  through required build edges. A closure that does not fit the remaining) Tj
T*
(  net budget defers the candidate under E_CAPACITY and leaves the closure) Tj
T*
(  members free to be admitted later on their own order position.) Tj
T*
(  A closure exactly equal to the remaining net budget fits. A closure one) Tj
T*
(  tick larger does not.) Tj
T*
(  Ranking units one at a time by priority, without pricing the closure,) Tj
T*
(  is not the documented objective.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A5. CROSS POOL PREREQUISITES) Tj
T*
(  A prerequisite in another pool is judged after every pool has been) Tj
T*
(  admitted. A selected unit whose cross pool required prerequisite is not) Tj
T*
(  selected is demoted to deferred under E_PREREQ_DEFERRED, and the demotion) Tj
T*
(  repeats until no selected unit has an unselected prerequisite. Capacity) Tj
T*
(  released by a demotion is not readmitted to the pool.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A6. CYCLE BREAKS) Tj
T*
(  A live cycle whose members form a breakable group loses one edge: the) Tj
T*
(  edge minimising \(break_cost, source, destination\), compared bytewise on) Tj
T*
(  the two identifiers. An edge with no declared break cost is not) Tj
T*
(  removable. A live cycle in a blocking group blocks every target the) Tj
T*
(  cycle is live on, and blocked units leave the schedule and the) Tj
T*
(  deployment manifest under E_CYCLE_BLOCKING.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A7. SCHEDULE TIE BREAK) Tj
T*
(  Among units ready at the same moment the order is \(priority_class,) Tj
T*
(  unit_id\) ascending, with unit_id compared bytewise.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
